Z||000002||Gold-86SE||08-08-2000||05:16 PM||||<BR>I have one, a recent purchase, but it is the project car for now.<P>Red on Gray exterior, Light Gray interior, automatic, cruise, moonroof, rear release, pw, pl.<P>Which means I now have an 84 SE 4-speed, 85 GT automatic, 86 SE 2.8 4-speed, and an 87 coupe (parts car).<P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 08-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||dman||08-08-2000||05:33 PM||||I have an 85 GT notchback.<P>It is a convertible, but otherwise it is stock: black paint with grey interior. It came with the older rims (the slotted ones that say Pontiac), not the lace/honeycomb (or whatever they're called). No spoiler.<P>It has been in storage since I got it (and prior to that it had been sitting for a few years). I'm gonna try and get it roadworthy once again within the next couple of months. Hopefully before the summer ends, but since I'm in Southern California it really doesn't make too much of a difference.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||cifc||08-08-2000||06:17 PM||||I picked up an 85 gt at an auction in June.  It hadn't been driven since 94.  I'm currently replacing the brakes and shocks/struts.  It should be driveable after that is done.  The paint is shot, but the interrior is almost perfect except for mismatched seats.||||reg||1
